nly on $[a,b]$, between the original limits","On $[\\alpha,\\beta]$, the interval of the parameter","Nowhere in particular, since $\\varphi'$ is continuous"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ecc6fe11361220cdc8d51b84","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_integration_by_substitution_type_2_8698067c_019_curated20261027_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which integral is suited to a Type 2 substitution $x=\\varphi(t)$ rather than to a Type 1 substitution or integration by parts?","options":["$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","$\\displaystyle\\int 2x\\cos(x^2)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","$\\displaystyle\\int x\\mathrm{e}^x\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","$\\displaystyle\\int_1^2\\frac{3x^2+2}{x^3+2x+3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"422100cd424da60b35132e2d","time_limit":25}]}}